# Serverless Functions

> **Full guide**: `docs/SERVERLESS_FUNCTIONS.md`. Step by step:
> `.claude/commands/create-function.md`.

- **Unit** = deployed Cloud Function (`functions/units.json`). **Dispatcher**
  = `callNodeFunction`, `identity`, `media` (one Node codebase in
  `functions/callNodeFunction`, three entry points) and `callPythonFunction`,
  routing by `Function-Name`. **Handler** = one routed function. Add
  handlers, not units; pick the Node dispatcher by the secrets the handler
  needs (Keycloak/Matrix → identity, storage only → media, else
  callNodeFunction; `docs/adr/0002-function-units-by-secret-scope.md`).
- Headers: `Hasura-Secret`, `Function-Name`, `Bucket`. The Node dispatchers
  and sendMail still accept the legacy `secret` / `name` until
  `docs/plans/functions-header-switch.md` is done; new metadata uses the
  standard names.
- Status codes: 401 secret, 404 unknown function, 500 server secret unset,
  400 (Node) conflicting names, 503 for a `retryable` event/cron failure,
  else 200 with `{ success, messageKey, error? }`.
- Node handlers read env via `lib/config.js`, Hasura via `lib/hasura.js`,
  HTTP via `lib/http.js`, the bucket via `lib/requestHeaders.js`.
- Register in `callNodeFunctionHandlers` / `identityHandlers` /
  `mediaHandlers` / `PYTHON_FUNCTIONS`; the registry test
  (`callNodeFunction/__tests__/registry.test.js`) checks each metadata entry
  calls the unit whose map holds the handler.
